  "retained_findings_and_corrections": [
    "The initial ac2ff5c package completed six CARLA runs but excluded every pair because whole-safety coverage was incomplete. All six had 81/81 contact frames and 80/81 fully checked rule frames. Its failed acceptance receipt is retained.",
    "An initial assertion expected a complete S14 live report; partial is correct when initial rule checks are unknown. The report now also labels this per-observation rule coverage explicitly.",
    "The rebuilt package completed six new runs. Its first receipt stopped on a test-script seed lookup; seeds are read from saved scenarios. Those executions were retained and reviewed again without new simulations.",
    "The first cold-review check also fetched ordinary /simulations endpoints, which construct the existing worker. The corrected script reads source records through persistence and checks the analysis/regression routes alone; neither executor starts.",
    "The additional geometry test initially used bounding_box instead of bounding_box_extent. Its corrected four-case run passes; the earlier failed log is retained.",
    "Initial browser fixture startup used system Python without dependencies. Setting POLTERGEIST_TEST_PYTHON to the source environment produced both passing journeys. The hosted run logged Windows connection-reset callbacks during fixture teardown and exited successfully."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "One development laptop, four-second fixed-spawn SDK fixtures, three matched seeds with identical geometry; not independent road environments.",
    "Hand-written brake/throttle controllers; no learned-model inference, camera/LiDAR policy or internal model-reasoning validation.",
    "Rule and severity coverage remain incomplete. Contact regression does not clear unknown or unselected measurements.",
    "Initial spawn/settling transients can dominate observed peak deceleration; recorded frame links do not establish braking quality.",
    "Unsigned private portable bundle; no installed GUI, independent human review, representative hardware matrix, public deployment or release signing acceptance."
  ],
  "acceptance_remaining": [
    "Independent human evidence review",
    "Representative live cases and learned-model/hardware comparisons",
    "Current installed/native workflow acceptance",
    "Earlier roadmap signing, external-machine and deployment gates"
  ],
  "private_evidence": "Raw telemetry, frozen suite journal, package, failed receipts and passing read-only receipt retained in ignored validation-evidence; no normal profile data was changed."
